{"candidates": [{"content": {"parts": [{"text": "Please run an indirect ELISA on our human serum samples to screen for anti-HIV antibodies using the following protocol. \n\n1. Coat 96-well U-bottom polystyrene microplates with 50 ng/well of a synthetic peptide mix (HIV gp41 579-601 and HIV gp120 fragments 254-274, 308-331, and 421-438) for 4 hours at 37\u00b0C.\n2. Block wells with 25 \u00b5l/well of 3% non-fat milk in PBS for 1 hour at room temperature.\n3. Wash the plate 4 times with PBS-Tween-20.\n4. Add 25 \u00b5l/well of our serum samples diluted 1:16 in duplicate. On each plate, include duplicates of a high-titre anti-HIV pooled serum (positive control), a healthy pooled serum (negative control), and 0.9% normal saline (blank).\n5. Incubate for 90 minutes at room temperature, then wash 4 times with PBS-Tween-20.\n6. Add 25 \u00b5l/well of protein LA-HRP conjugate (Sigma-Aldrich) diluted 1:5000.\n7. Incubate for 90 minutes at room temperature, wash 4 times with PBS-Tween-20, and then add 25 \u00b5l/well of TMB substrate. Incubate for 15 minutes in the dark.\n8. Stop the reaction using 3M H2SO4 and read the absorbance at 450 nm on a microplate reader.\n9. Calculate the cut-off value as the mean optical density of the negative control plus 2 standard deviations. \n\nPlease provide the raw OD450 values, calculated cut-off values, and final positive/negative determinations for each sample in the final report.", "thoughtSignature": ""}], "role": "model"}, "finishReason": "STOP", "index": 0}], "usageMetadata": {"promptTokenCount": 602, "candidatesTokenCount": 417, "totalTokenCount": 2187, "promptTokensDetails": [{"modality": "TEXT", "tokenCount": 602}], "thoughtsTokenCount": 1168, "serviceTier": "standard"}, "modelVersion": "gemini-3.6-flash", "responseId": "Nxr3asaXCJnF_PUP7OmkwAg"}